# Repository Unit Testing Rules

## Core Setup Patterns

### Basic Repository Test Setup
```php
protected Mockery\MockInterface $repository;
protected Mockery\MockInterface $context;
protected Mockery\MockInterface $eloquentBuilder;
protected Mockery\MockInterface $policy;
protected Mockery\MockInterface $repositoryModel;

protected function setUp(): void
{
    parent::setUp();

    // Model mock with proper class concatenation
    $this->repositoryModel = Mockery::mock(Model::class . ',' . Model::class)
        ->shouldAllowMockingProtectedMethods();

    // Repository mock with partial implementation
    $this->repository = Mockery::mock(Repository::class)
        ->makePartial()
        ->shouldAllowMockingProtectedMethods();

    $this->eloquentBuilder = Mockery::mock(Builder::class);

    // Prepare repository for mocking
    $this->repository->prepareForMocking($this->repositoryModel);

    // Common setup for query builder
    $this->repositoryModel->shouldReceive('newQuery')
        ->andReturn($this->eloquentBuilder);

    $this->repositoryModel->shouldReceive('getTable')
        ->andReturn('table_name');

    // Setup policy mock
    $this->policy = $this->mock(Policy::class);

    // Setup global scope handling
    $this->repositoryModel->shouldReceive('addGlobalScope')
        ->zeroOrMoreTimes();
}
```

## Query Builder Mocking

### Where Clause Pattern
```php
$this->eloquentBuilder->shouldReceive('where')
    ->with('column', '=', $value)
    ->andReturnSelf();
```

### WhereIn Pattern
```php
$this->eloquentBuilder->shouldReceive('whereIn')
    ->withSomeOfArgs('column')
    ->andReturnSelf();
```

### Join Pattern
```php
$this->eloquentBuilder->shouldReceive('join')
    ->with('table', 'first.id', '=', 'second.id')
    ->andReturnSelf();
```

### Relationship Loading
```php
$this->eloquentBuilder->shouldReceive('with')
    ->with(['relation1', 'relation2'])
    ->andReturnSelf();
```

## Policy Testing

### Authorization Check Pattern
```php
$this->policy->shouldReceive('methodName')
    ->with($this->context, $model)
    ->andReturn(true|false);

$this->context->shouldReceive('can')
    ->with('permission', [$model])
    ->andReturn(true|false);
```

## Reference Parameter Handling

### Method with Reference Parameter
```php
$this->repository->shouldReceive('methodName')
    ->with(
        Mockery::on(function ($arg) use ($expectedArg) {
            return $arg === $expectedArg;
        }),
        Mockery::on(function (&$arg) {
            return true;
        })
    )
    ->andReturnUsing(function ($param1, &$param2) {
        $param2 = ['modified' => 'value'];
    });
```

## Event Handling

### Event Dispatcher Pattern
```php
$dispatcher = Mockery::mock(Dispatcher::class);

$dispatcher->shouldReceive('dispatch')
    ->with('event.name', [$param], true)
    ->once();

$this->app->extend('events', fn () => $dispatcher);
```

## Common Test Patterns

### CRUD Operation Tests
1. Create Operation
```php
public function testCreate(): void
{
    // Setup attributes
    $attributes = ['key' => 'value'];

    // Mock policy check
    $this->policy->shouldReceive('create')
        ->andReturn(true);

    // Mock model creation
    $this->repository->shouldReceive('getModel')
        ->andReturn($model);

    $result = $this->repository->create($this->context, $attributes);
    $this->assertInstanceOf(Model::class, $result);
}
```

2. Update Operation
```php
public function testUpdate(): void
{
    $this->eloquentBuilder->shouldReceive('find')
        ->with($id)
        ->andReturn($model);

    $this->policy->shouldReceive('update')
        ->andReturn(true);

    $result = $this->repository->update($this->context, $id, $attributes);
    $this->assertInstanceOf(Model::class, $result);
}
```

3. Delete Operation
```php
public function testDelete(): void
{
    $this->repository->shouldReceive('find')
        ->with($id)
        ->andReturn($model);

    Queue::fake();
    $result = $this->repository->delete($this->context, $id);
    Queue::assertPushed(DeleteJob::class);
}
```

### Pagination Tests
```php
public function testPagination(): void
{
    $this->eloquentBuilder->shouldReceive('paginate')
        ->andReturn(Mockery::mock(Paginator::class));

    $result = $this->repository->paginate($params);
    $this->assertInstanceOf(Paginator::class, $result);
}
```

## Best Practices

### Test Method Organization
1. Group related tests together
2. Use descriptive test method names
3. Test both success and edge cases
4. Mock only what's necessary
5. Use helper methods for common setup

### Test Attributes
1. Use `#[DoesNotPerformAssertions]` for void methods
2. Add proper assertions for return values
3. Test both success and failure cases

### Error Handling
1. Test exception cases
2. Verify error responses
3. Test validation failures

### Mock Cleanup
```php
protected function tearDown(): void
{
    unset(
        $this->repository,
        $this->context,
        $this->eloquentBuilder,
        $this->policy,
        $this->repositoryModel
    );
    parent::tearDown();
}
```

## Common Assertions

### Instance Assertions
```php
$this->assertInstanceOf(ExpectedClass::class, $result);
$this->assertInstanceOf(Paginator::class, $result);
$this->assertInstanceOf(Builder::class, $result);
```

### Value Assertions
```php
$this->assertTrue($result);
$this->assertFalse($result);
$this->assertNull($result);
$this->assertEquals($expected, $actual);
$this->assertIsArray($result);
```

### Exception Assertions
```php
$this->expectException(AuthorizationException::class);
$this->expectException(ValidationException::class);
```
